  <name>Steuererklärung</name>
  <!-- TRANSLATORS: One line, no full stop: what the app does for the person using it -->
  <summary>Bookkeeping and tax returns for a small German business</summary>
  <description>
    <!-- TRANSLATORS: Opening paragraph: what the app does. Keep EÜR and ELSTER as they are. -->
    <p>Receipts, bookings and invoices in one place — and out of them the German income surplus statement (EÜR), the VAT return, trade tax and the partnership assessment, as ELSTER XML or transmitted directly.</p>
    <!-- TRANSLATORS: Second paragraph: the app works without AI, and the AI boundary -->
    <p>Fully usable without AI: your own classification rules instead of guessing, and every figure traceable down to the booking it came from. An assistant can help, but it never books anything by itself.</p>
    <!-- TRANSLATORS: Bullet list of what the app does -->
    <ul>
      <!-- TRANSLATORS: Feature list: import and classification -->
      <li>Import bank statements and receipts, classify them by your own rules</li>
      <!-- TRANSLATORS: Feature list: invoicing. Keep XRechnung and ZUGFeRD as they are. -->
      <li>Write invoices as PDF and e-invoice (XRechnung, ZUGFeRD)</li>
      <!-- TRANSLATORS: Feature list: the tax forms. Keep EÜR as it is. -->
      <li>Compute EÜR, VAT return, trade tax and the partnership assessment</li>
      <!-- TRANSLATORS: Feature list: ELSTER submission. Keep ELSTER as it is. -->
      <li>Transmit to the tax office through ELSTER, or export the XML and keep it</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
